Two parallel metal plates in a vacuum are separated by 0.045 m. A potential difference V is applied between the plates, as shown in Fig. 5.1.
{{figure:figure_5_1.png}}
A proton is initially at rest on the surface of the positive plate. The proton in the uniform electric field takes a time of 1.5 × 10⁻⁷ s to reach the negative plate.
